✅ 4. Can we write
Object lock = new Object();

inside the method?

public void increment(){
    Object lock = new Object();
    synchronized(lock){

    }
}

Answer ❌ No.

Every method call creates a new lock object.

Example

Thread-A
↓
Lock-1
Thread-B
↓
Lock-2
Different monitors.

No synchronization occurs between the threads.